        kind: 'faded',
        text: 'A plastics plant keeps an €80,000 spare gearbox for its main extruder (the machine that melts and pushes plastic through a die). The extruder runs 24/7 and loses €1,500 of margin per hour when it stops. A new gearbox takes 14 weeks to deliver.\n\nBased on the plant’s history, the gearbox fails about once in 20 years. Holding cost is 20% per year. The finance controller wants to sell the spare to free up working capital, the cash tied up in stock.',
